  "notes": [
    "Git hashes cover the deterministic tar stream produced by git archive at the pinned commit, before applying recorded patches. They are not GitHub tarball hashes.",
    "NuGet and MoltenVK archive hashes come from the previously verified offline inputs. No network was used to create this lock.",
    "The nxnative and nx2apple-patches rows moved on 2026-11-05 (engine pin f8a5618d, published queue 8d13135e). Those two commits were cloned from their public GitHub repositories for that move, the only network use; each hash is of git archive --format=tar COMMIT from the clone. Four queue patches are replaced by the tracked ports in scripts/deps/upstream/nxnative-queue.",
    "MoltenVK release archives supply SPIRV-Tools, SPIRV-Headers, Vulkan-Headers and cereal internally; notices and revisions are in Tools/VulkanBackend/Notices/manifest.json.",
    "Missing hashes are explicit blockers, never trust-on-first-use pins.",
    "Ryujinx 1.3.3 is a reference only, not a build input. Since 2026-11-05 the game shader translator builds from the MIT Ryujinx shader sources the nxnative row vendors (223 files pinned in Tools/MaxwellShaderCompiler/game-source-lock.json). The nx2apple-translator row (8227f80f) remains for the original fixture framework and the interpreter-era libraries.",
    "NX2Apple repositories include bundled dependencies with their own retained notices, including libvpx (BSD), dav1d (BSD 2-Clause), stb_vorbis (MIT/public domain), bcdec (MIT), Vulkan headers (Apache-2.0 or MIT) and Ryujinx (MIT). The bootstrap does not fetch separate copies.",
    "Tool source pins use upstream source URLs, not Homebrew bottles. They are separated from exercised inputs: source archive verification and standalone tool recipes remain unvalidated. The local diagnostic route still uses installed executables."
  ],
